# Warehouse data NEVER enters this repo. Not in a private one, not once, not
# "temporarily" — git history is permanent and a repo is a new copy under new
# access control. Input bundles move out-of-band and live wherever
# BOOTSTRAP_FIXTURES points.
data/
fixtures/
# tests/fixtures/ is the exception, and it is not warehouse data: a four-model dbt
# project written for this repo, which the export round trip needs on a fresh
# clone. `fixtures/` above kept it untracked, so the suite passed here and would
# have failed for anyone else.
!tests/fixtures/
*/input/
*/workspace*/
*.duckdb

# Run artifacts: regenerable from the inputs, and they contain warehouse content.
run/
run-*/
*-run/
packets/
profile/
briefs/
decisions/
cassis/
workspace/
QUESTIONS.md
TREE.md
questions*.yml
questions*.md
verify_*.json
judge_*.json
*_findings.json
column_glossary.json
column_comments.json
declared_keys.json
scope-proposed.tsv
prefill_report.json
batches.json
joins_draft.yml
# Run configs name YOUR paths. intake.py writes them here, and a config that
# reached the tree carried an absolute home directory into a repo meant to be
# copied to a public one — a leak neither the customer-name tier nor the
# identifier tier of the release gate can see. Only the example ships.
configs/*.yml
!configs/example.yml

docs-packets/
docs_candidates.json
docs_answers.yml
docs_score.json

# Gold / evaluation material: the answers.
gold*/
gold*.json
scope-gold*.txt
scope-*.txt
fixture*.csv
test-cases/
verdicts.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.venv/
